WEBVTT

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:05.650
Amiya!

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.400
I won't let you!

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.410
I will... protect everyone!

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.330
Oh?

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.720
Amiya! Stop!

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.220
Dobermann!

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:29.340
Hurry! Get everyone out of here!

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.050
You want us to leave you?!

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.840
You can't handle her by yourself!

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.390
Amiya! Don't do it!

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.390
If you try, your rings...

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.930
Even if my body gets 
shredded to pieces... I'll...

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.990
I see.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.260
So it's you.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.400
All units, fire on Talulah.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.800
Cover Amiya.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:47.890
Ace...

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.360
You all right?!

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.260
Why did they stop? 
Is this part of their plan?

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.780
<i>We don't have time to dawdle.</i>

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:02.510
Right.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.570
<i>All units, follow orders and evacuate!</i>

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:07.470
<i>Doctor, you have command.</i>

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:08.330
Roger.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.210
<i>There's a gap in the rubble of the 
collapsed buildings. Go through that.</i>

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:19.590
<i>Once you're out of the square, there's a 
place you can hide close to the evac zone.</i>

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.360
What do we do?

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.070
Help me...

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.050
<i>Calm down! Don't panic!</i>

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.620
Help me...

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.790
Are we gonna die here?

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:47.790
Help me!

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:50.660
I don't want to die... I don't want to die!

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:54.670
All units! Stay close!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.000
Amiya!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.050
This is... as much as I can cover!

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.200
T-Talulah!

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:15.520
It hurts... It hurts!

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.440
My arm! My arm!

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.930
She's ignoring her allies' pleas?

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.570
Amiya! Are you all right?

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:28.390
We're past the peak. Let's get 
going before the second wave.

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.160
Nearl, you lead the way.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.060
Got it.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.000
You're letting your guard down, Amiya.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.000
Retreat! Run!

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:40.710
Hurry!

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:45.840
You okay?!

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.350
Dammit! The stretcher's broken!

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.010
I'll hold Talulah—

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:50.850
Amiya!

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.850
I'll hold her here. 
Take the Doctor and leave!

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.490
Capt. Dobermann, go!

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:57.860
We'll handle this somehow!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:00.390
Don't worry about us. 
We'll be right behind you.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.100
Roger that!

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.360
Where are Ace's people?!

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.160
They're keeping Talulah occupied...

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.300
It's not safe here. Let's move—

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.010
No! You can't!

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.270
Ace!

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:13.790
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:14.950
Ace!

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.670
I'll clear a path...

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.060
Amiya!

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:20.240
<i>Get going!</i>

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.510
But...

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:24.050
<i>We'll be fine. Go.</i>

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.970
<i>"Think about what to prioritize," right?</i>

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:32.820
<i>I'm counting on you, Dobermann.</i>

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:37.940
Roger.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.700
Back in formation! Forward!

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:43.700
<i>Doctor.</i>

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:51.990
<i>There will come a day when you and Amiya
have to make a stand against this cruel world.</i>

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.500
<i>Take care of her. I'm counting on you.</i>

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.500
Got it.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:01.270
<i>Now go. Good luck!</i>

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.340
Looks like the Catastrophe's over...

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.730
It's a good thing the 
exfiltration point's clear.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:17.970
Let's wait here till our transport comes. 
Stay alert to our surroundings.

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:20.840
Nearl.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:23.720
"The Radiant Knight...

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.120
must always be the noble light that 
illuminates the way forward for the people."

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.160
That's what you said before, isn't it?

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.490
Yes, I know.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.160
I can't let their efforts go to waste.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:41.800
Amiya.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:42.900
Doctor...

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.880
Where's Ace's team? Are they all right?

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:56.180
I see...

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.270
It's okay.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:09.030
I'm sure Ace will be fine.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:14.030
Everyone at Rhodes Island is very strong.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:26.300
What drives you to these 
lengths? I don't get it.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.900
He's fighting to his very last breath.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.300
That's a true warrior.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.200
I'll remember you, Rhodes Island.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:40.730
I finally found you!

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.730
I didn't think it'd be smooth 
sailing from here on out...

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:49.740
Why don't we introduce 
ourselves to break the ice?

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.740
You can call me W.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.430
"W"?

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.740
Have we met before?

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:00.750
Maybe.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.500
W! What do you want?!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.420
What do I want? Let's see...

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.300
How about you hand over the Doctor?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.400
You know the Doctor?

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:17.300
I sure do! I came to this hellhole 
just to enjoy a touching little reunion.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:22.160
This isn't even worth discussing. 
Amiya, let's not waste time on her.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.310
Ah, so your name's Amiya.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:27.810
Well, whatever. I got what I came for.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.590
We'll see each other again, little bunny.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.000
Let's go.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.610
H-Hey!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.530
See ya.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.760
Hold it!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.170
Are they really just leaving?

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.510
Yes... It felt like something was up, though.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.340
Hey, you okay?

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:57.340
Capt. Ace...

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.430
Where is everyone?

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:02.720
It's just you and me now.

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.510
No way...

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:07.650
I...

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:11.210
All I could do... was scream...

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.610
I couldn't... do anything!

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.400
I'm... sorry...

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.260
Calm down. You'll open your wounds.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:27.370
I patched you up.
 You should be able to walk soon.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.380
Captain!

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.820
Your arm!

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.130
It's okay. I've got another one.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.310
Captain, you should run!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:39.760
You can make it out! I'm sure of—

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.760
No, not yet.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.840
The transport should be arriving 
at the evac zone soon.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.890
It's all over if they get spotted.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:47.610
I'll buy them time.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:48.970
Then, I'm coming too—

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:56.220
Guard, I traded my arm for your life.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.690
Live on.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:04.410
I have to know that... 
it was a worthwhile trade.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:06.320
I'll be right back.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.780
Capt. Ace!

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:16.420
I'm... such... a failure!

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:36.520
What's wrong?

00:10:40.150 --> 00:10:41.570
My heart...

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.750
It kind of hurts a little...

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.330
Medic...

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:56.710
Don't cry... please...

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:55.710
Why?!

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:01.370
A long time ago, someone told me something...

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:07.860
"After a battle, we have to hold back the 
tears until we're at home by ourselves."

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.230
Let's go.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.890
We're going home... to Rhodes Island.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.220
You're looking at that cluster, right?

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:47.470
That's Originium, too.

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:49.980
It's like what you saw in the square.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:54.940
The Originium crashes down to the ground
 like meteors. That's what Catastrophes are.

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:59.730
Depending on the region, Catastrophes 
can take the form of blizzards or floods,

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.490
but they always leave behind Originium.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.910
They're that big?

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:08.720
Originium grows on the ground.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:11.540
It grows? But it's a mineral.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.500
I don't know the exact details,

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:21.440
but the crystal veins eventually rupture 
and release Originium particles.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:26.010
They gather in the sky and form clouds, 
eventually causing a new Catastrophe.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:29.260
It's just like... Oripathy...

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:33.690
Right, it's just like the 
fate that awaits us Infected.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:38.160
Catastrophes, Oripathy, 
and the human hate...

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.990
They all spread to no end—

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:40.990
Dobermann.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.940
You're tired, aren't you?

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.390
You'd better rest up.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.950
Thanks for your concern.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.090
Don't worry, though.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:54.300
I'd rather talk to loosen up.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.750
I see... You're right.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.570
Doctor, sorry for forcing 
this conversation on you.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:04.240
No... You're helping me.

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:07.760
Can you still see Chernobog?

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.060
Yes.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:14.150
The city is built on top 
of a large mobility device.

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:18.070
In other words, the entire city can move.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:21.130
So that it can avoid Catastrophes?

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:26.030
That's right. Most cities in 
the world are nomadic cities.

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:29.950
It's possible to predict 
where a Catastrophe will occur.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:33.970
You can avoid disaster by moving 
your city out of the way in advance.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:37.540
Then, why didn't Chernobog...

00:13:38.590 --> 00:13:39.600
Good question.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:44.050
There might be something 
sinister behind this uprising.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:50.530
Are those people heading to Rhodes Island?

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.560
No, they're probably going to Lungmen.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:56.350
Lungmen?

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.530
They're likely headed for a city up ahead.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:02.860
My guess is they're Infected who 
managed to get out of Chernobog.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:06.150
<i>This is your pilot speaking. 
We will be landing momentarily.</i>

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.530
Welcome back.

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:55.980
We returned safely.

00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:58.410
I heard what happened.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.080
It was a tough mission, wasn't it?

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:02.420
Yes...

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:06.000
Nearl! Thank goodness you're okay.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:10.560
Thanks. Sorry, can someone 
get me a stretcher?

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.000
I'll get one right away!

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.140
Thank you so much.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.800
We'll help out, too.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:19.560
Is the Doctor okay?

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:21.770
Out like a light.

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:25.570
Must've calmed down after 
we landed at Rhodes Island.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:30.150
We really pushed the Doctor to the limit.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:32.670
Doctor...

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:49.050
<i>Are you awake, Doctor?</i>

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.170
Where am I?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.560
<i>This is the reception room.</i>

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:58.930
<i>Your room is still being prepared, 
so we had you rest here.</i>

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.690
<i>Oh, of course, we're still on 
the Rhodes Island landship.</i>

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.400
<i>You may continue to rest if you like.</i>

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.060
I want to head outside.

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:12.450
<i>In that case, I will take you to Amiya.</i>

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.750
You're a smart one.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:17.440
<i>I am no match for you, Doctor.</i>

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.790
<i>There is a change of clothes for you there.</i>

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:23.900
<i>Amiya is currently on the deck.</i>

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:27.170
<i>It is some distance from here.</i>

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:32.800
<i>As we make our way there, allow me to familiarize
 you with the different facilities on the ship.</i>

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:34.180
Thanks.

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:46.690
<i>Rhodes Island is sailing 
toward its next destination.</i>

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.580
<i>Is something the matter?</i>

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:54.020
I... really don't know...

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.700
My...

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:01.840
My present... and future.

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.600
Lead the way.

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:08.980
<i>Leave it to me.</i>

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:15.590
<i>Rhodes Island is a landship equipped 
with a variety of medical facilities.</i>

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.600
<i>From the most advanced surgeries 
to drug prescriptions,</i>

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:23.730
<i>we have everything, even special equipment
 used specifically in Oripathy research.</i>

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.400
<i>All energy necessary for our 
operations is generated within the ship.</i>

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:31.150
<i>The landship mines and refines the 
Originium used in power generation.</i>

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:36.080
<i>We also process Originium, 
as well as other heavy metals</i>

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:39.490
<i>for trading with cities and corporations.</i>

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:43.910
<i>The living quarters were designed 
for the comfort and wellbeing</i>

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.050
<i>of our Operators and inpatients,</i>

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:48.970
<i>and can help alleviate the 
mental and physical stress</i>

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:52.420
<i>accumulated during 
missions and treatments.</i>

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:55.680
<i>Here at Rhodes Island, 
a great number of us live together,</i>

00:17:55.680 --> 00:18:01.430
<i>regardless of each individual's 
background, race, or infection status.</i>

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:05.390
<i>Furthermore, owing to the broad spectrum 
of Rhodes Island's activities,</i>

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:10.190
<i>we also provide transport as well as 
a variety of weapons and equipment.</i>

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:17.400
<i>We have arrived at our destination. 
May I conclude this tour?</i>

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:19.500
Thanks. That was a great help.

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.950
The weight she carries on her shoulders...

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:27.350
is so heavy.

00:18:33.600 --> 00:18:34.540
Amiya.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.440
Doctor.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:41.060
Shouldn't you be in bed?

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.300
It's okay.

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:46.410
I'm wide awake.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:48.060
Me, too.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:51.760
I couldn't sleep, so I came 
outside for some fresh air.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:57.820
I can't stop thinking 
about what Talulah said.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:03.930
It's true. I may be an idealist 
full of empty promises.

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:08.330
Even so, I want to believe 
that I've chosen the right path.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:15.920
But... I've also had doubts 
about the path I've chosen.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:20.340
I think she might've noticed that...

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.180
I'm sorry.

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:26.850
You probably don't know what 
to say, hearing this from me.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:32.850
Ace told me something
 in his last transmission.

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:41.610
He said there would come a day when you and 
I have to make a stand against this cruel world.

00:19:43.310 --> 00:19:46.970
I don't really understand 
what he meant by that yet.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:52.940
If you persevere with your ideals, 
you will surely clash with reality...

00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:59.470
Even so, he... he believed that you 
would press forward on the right path.

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:01.630
Ace...

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.130
You're right.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.640
I shouldn't let myself lose sight of my path.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:13.070
I may be an empty shell right now,

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:15.650
but I'll complete myself, bit by bit.

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:17.760
Then...

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:21.770
I promise I will help you
 realize your ideals.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.660
Thank you, Doctor.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.220
But please don't push yourself.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:31.660
We'll have a new mission in three days.

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:37.980
Be sure to rest up and recover 
your strength until then.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.130
I will.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:48.180
Let's get started, then.

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:50.960
During the Chernobog operation,

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:54.190
we fulfilled our primary objective: 
the exfiltration of the Doctor.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:56.690
Albeit with great losses.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:00.430
Nonetheless, we learned 
a great deal about Reunion.

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:03.190
You could say it was a success, 
strategically speaking.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:10.440
Based on our analysis, we can determine that 
Reunion's next target is Lungmen in Yan.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.200
Lungmen...

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.640
It's not as draconian as Chernobog,

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:18.710
but Lungmen treats its Infected 
populace pretty harshly, too.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:25.430
Regarding that, Dr. Kal'tsit has already left for 
Lungmen to prepare a contract with its leader.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:29.450
One that allows Rhodes Island to operate
 openly inside Lungmen's borders,

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:31.430
though exact terms haven't been agreed yet.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:35.420
That's why, Doctor, we'd like 
you and Amiya to head to Lungmen

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:38.940
and work with Dr. Kal'tsit 
to get this contract signed.

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:44.410
Once that's done, your mission is to 
investigate Reunion's activities in Lungmen.

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:45.450
Understood.

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:48.710
Nearl will come with me on another mission.

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:49.950
Okay.

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:52.950
There's no telling what 
Reunion's next step is.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:55.360
Be extra careful.

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:56.020
Right.

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:58.580
Doctor.

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:03.460
I look forward to working with you again.

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:06.460
Me, too.
